# Prisma & Database

Prisma is the only ORM unless an explicit project decision says otherwise. Never call Prisma from portal/web client code.

## Before new models

Inspect schema → search equivalents → reuse relations → add indexes for query patterns → unique constraints where needed. Prefer `createdAt` / `updatedAt` / `createdBy` / `updatedBy`. Use enums for finite statuses — not arbitrary strings.

## Performance (100K–1M+ rows)

Pagination (cursor where useful), selective fields, efficient joins, batch ops, DB aggregation. Never load entire survey tables into memory. Avoid `SELECT *` on list APIs. Index composite filters (ward, date, status, etc.).

## Integrity

FKs, uniques, transactions, enums. Careful with cascading deletes. Prefer soft delete where justified. Never casually delete payments, financial rows, or audit logs — prefer immutable financial history.

## Migrations

Use Prisma migrations. Inspect impact before applying. No destructive production shortcuts without explicit approval. No random manual schema edits if migrations are the established path.
